      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-11T03:41:11.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't know… Put into play is effectively the same as playing, except that it gets around the \"cannot play\" restriction… I would say it WOULD force a shuffle. I haven't seen otherwise confirmed officially, at least.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>We do have it officially confirmed. You resuffle on Play, Draw, or Discard. Put into Play does none of these.</p>",
