      "raw": "I didn't say it WASN'T, I said I hadn't SEEN it. My interpretation was that play, discard, and draw effects were examples, (\"it does on these things,\" not, \"it does EXCLUSIVELY on these things\") usually given in the context of, \"reveal doesn't force a shuffle, but these are some things that do.\" \r\n\r\nIn fact, the only official word I've seen is that reveals don't force a shuffle. So, I would say the ruling is ambiguous. Unless, of course, you can point me to where they said that EVERYTHING that is not explicitly, \"play, draw, or discard\" does not force a shuffle (as opposed to them saying that a SPECIFIC action that is not one of those things, like revealing, doesn't.)",
