      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>The more I look at this, the more it doesn&#39;t make sense.&nbsp; Spiff&#39;s clarifications state that Play, Draw, and Discard always trigger a shuffle.&nbsp; Just because it says &quot;Play the top card&quot;, that doesn&#39;t mean it&#39;s not playing a card.&nbsp; If there is no top card, shouldn&#39;t there be a shuffle in order to play a card?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This language has been around since the beginning.&nbsp; Citizen Dawn&#39;s Channel the Eclipse has &quot;Play the top card of the villain deck&quot;.&nbsp; Atlantean Font of Power -&nbsp; &quot;At the end of the environment turn, play the top card of the villain deck.&nbsp; Play the top card of each hero deck in turn order.&nbsp; If the played card is a limited card already in play, discard that card and play the next card.&nbsp;&nbsp; At the start of the environment turn, destroy this card.&quot;&nbsp; So the way it is worded, play the top card is the same as play the next card.&nbsp; And both of those are synonymous with Play a card.&nbsp; For the heroes, it is worded that way in order to distinguish playing a card from your hand.&nbsp;</p><p>So unless&nbsp;someone can point to a clarification somewhere that states that playing the top card is not the same as playing a card off the deck, then I&#39;ll have to go with Spiff&#39;s clarifications.&nbsp; Thanks in advance.</p>",
